G3606.b:
⟪ὅθεν⟫ adv., ⟪whence⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of direction or source: ⟦Matthew 12:44|Mt 12:44⟧, ⟦Luke 11:24|Lk 11:24⟧, ⟦Acts 14:26|Ac 14:26⟧ ⟦Acts 28:13|28:13⟧; = ἐκεῖθεν ὅπου, ⟦Matthew 25:24|Mt 25:24⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:26|26⟧ (cf. Thuc., i, 89, 3); ὅ. γινώσκομεν, ⟦1 John 2:18|I Jo 2:18⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of cause, ⟪whence⟫, ⟪wherefore⟫: ⟦Matthew 14:7|Mt 14:7⟧, ⟦Acts 26:19|Ac 26:19⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:17|He 2:17⟧ ⟦Hebrews 3:1|3:1⟧ ⟦Hebrews 7:25|7:25⟧ ⟦Hebrews 8:3|8:3⟧ ⟦Hebrews 9:18|9:18⟧ ⟦Hebrews 11:19|11:19⟧.†

G3609.b:
⟪οἰκεῖος⟫, -α, -ον
(< οἶκος), [in LXX for ⁨דּוֹד⁩, ⁨שְׁאֵר⁩, etc.; in ⟦Isaiah 58:7|Is 58:7⟧, οἰ. τοῦ σπέρματος for ⁨בָּשָׂר⁩;] ⟪in⟫ or ⟪of the house⟫ (opp. to ξένος, ἀλλότριος);
⟪(a)⟫ of things; τὰ οἰ., ⟪household affairs⟫ or ⟪goods⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ of persons, ⟪of the same family⟫ or ⟪kin⟫; as subst., οἱ οἰ., ⟪kinsmen⟫: ⟦1 Timothy 5:8|I Ti 5:8⟧; c. gen. pers., ⟪of the family of⟫: metaph., τ. θεοῦ, ⟦Ephesians 2:19|Eph 2:19⟧; τ. πίστεως (Lft., in l.), ⟦Galatians 6:10|Ga 6:10⟧.†
SYN.: συγγενής, ἴδιος (v. Cremer, 446; Deiss., BS., 123).

G3614.b:
⟪οἰκία⟫, -ας, ἡ
(< οἶκος), [in LXX chiefly (very freq.) for ⁨בַּיִת⁩;] ⟪a house⟫, ⟪dwelling⟫: ⟦Matthew 2:11|Mt 2:11⟧ ⟦Matthew 7:24|7:24-27⟧, ⟦Mark 1:29|Mk 1:29⟧, al.; ἐν οἰκίᾳ (= cl. κατ ̓ οἰκίαν), ⟪at home⟫, ⟦Luke 8:27|Lk 8:27⟧; εἰς οἰ., ⟦2 John 1:10|II Jo 10⟧; οἰ, c. gen. pers., usually has the art. (⟦Matthew 8:14|Mt 8:14⟧, al., but cf. οἶκος and v. Bl., § 46, 9); ἡ οἰ. τ. πατρός μου, ⟦John 14:2|Jo 14:2⟧. Metaph.,
⟪(a)⟫ of the body as the dwelling of the soul: ⟦2 Corinthians 5:1|II Co 5:1⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of property (as ⁨בַּיִת⁩, ⟦Genesis 45:18|Ge 45:18⟧, LXX, τ. ὑπάρχοντα; ⟦1 Kings 13:8|III Ki 13:8⟧, LXX, οἶκος) = οἶκος (q.v.): ⟦Mark 12:40|Mk 12:40⟧, ⟦Luke 20:47|Lk 20:47⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of the inmates of the dwelling, ⟪the household⟫: ⟦Matthew 12:25|Mt 12:25⟧; c. gen. pers., ⟦John 4:53|Jo 4:53⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:15|I Co 16:15⟧.
SYN.: οἶκος, which in Attic law denoted the whole estate, οἰκία, the dwelling only. In cl. poets οἶκος has also the latter sense, but not in prose, except in metaph. usage, where it signifies both property and household. The foregoing distinction is not, however, consistently maintained in late Greek; cf. MM, ii, xvii, and v. Thayer, s.v. οἰκία.

G3625.b:
⟪οἰκουμένη⟫, -ης, ἡ
(fem. pres. pass. ptcp. of οἰκέω; sc. γῆ), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨תֵּבֵל⁩, ⁨אֶרֶץ⁩;] ⟪the inhabited earth⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in cl., the countries occupied by Greeks, as disting. from barbarian lands (Hdt., Dem., al.);
⟪(b)⟫ in later writers, the Roman world: ⟦Luke 2:1|Lk 2:1⟧, ⟦Acts 11:28|Ac 11:28⟧ ⟦Acts 24:5|24:5⟧; by meton., of its inhabitants: ⟦Acts 17:6|Ac 17:6⟧ ⟦Acts 19:27|19:27⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ in LXX (⟦Psalms 23:1|Ps 22 (23):1⟧ ⟦Psalms 71:8|70 (71):8⟧, al.) and NT, also of the whole inhabited world: ⟦Matthew 24:14|Mt 24:14⟧, ⟦Luke 4:5|Lk 4:5⟧ ⟦Luke 21:26|21:26⟧, ⟦Romans 10:18|Ro 10:18⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:6|He 1:6⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:10|Re 3:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:14|16:14⟧; by meton. (ut supr.), ⟦Acts 17:31|Ac 17:31⟧, ⟦Revelation 12:9|Re 12:9⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ of the Messianic age, ἡ οἰ. ἡ μέλλουσα = ὁ αἰὼ ὁ μέλλων: ⟦Hebrews 2:5|He 2:5⟧.†

G3650.b:
⟪ὅλος⟫, -η, -ον,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨כֹּל⁩;] of persons and things, ⟪whole⟫, ⟪entire⟫, ⟪complete⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of indefinite ideas, c. subst. anarth.: ⟦Luke 5:5|Lk 5:5⟧, ⟦Acts 11:26|Ac 11:26⟧ ⟦Acts 28:30|28:30⟧, ⟦Titus 1:11|Tit 1:11⟧; ὅλον ἄνθρωπον (an entire man; v. Field, Notes, 93), ⟦John 7:23|Jo 7:23⟧; ὅλη Ἰερουσαλήμ (= πᾶσα Ἰ, ⟦Matthew 2:3|Mt 2:3⟧; v. Bl., § 47, 9), ⟦Acts 21:31|Ac 21:31⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Definite, c. art.;
	⟪(a)⟫ preceding subst.: ⟦Matthew 4:23|Mt 4:23⟧, ⟦Matthew 4:24|24⟧, ⟦Luke 8:39|Lk 8:39⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:17|I Co 12:17⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ following subst.: ⟦Mark 1:33|Mk 1:33⟧, ⟦Luke 9:25|Lk 9:25⟧, ⟦John 4:53|Jo 4:53⟧, ⟦Acts 21:30|Ac 21:30⟧, al.;
	⟪(c)⟫ between art. and subst., where subst. is an abstract noun (Plat., al.).
⟪3.⟫ Attached to adj. or verb: ⟦Matthew 13:33|Mt 13:33⟧, ⟦Luke 13:21|Lk 13:21⟧, ⟦John 9:34|Jo 9:34⟧, al.; adverbially, δι ̓ ὅλου (MM, xviii), ⟦John 19:23|Jo 19:23⟧.

G3667.b:
⟪ὁμοίωμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< ὁμοιόω), [in LXX for ⁨דְּמוּת⁩, ⁨תַּבְנִית⁩, ⁨תְּמוּנָה⁩, etc.;] ⟪that which is made like⟫ something;
⟪(a)⟫ concrete, ⟪an image⟫, ⟪likeness⟫ (⟦Psalms 106:20|Ps 105 (106):20⟧, ⟦Ezekiel 1:5|Ez 1:5⟧, I Mac 3:48, al.): ⟦Revelation 9:7|Re 9:7⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ abstract, ⟪likeness⟫, ⟪resemblance⟫: ⟦Romans 5:14|Ro 5:14⟧ ⟦Romans 6:5|6:5⟧ ⟦Romans 8:3|8:3⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:7|Phl 2:7⟧; ἐν ὁ. εἰκόνος, ⟦Romans 1:23|Ro 1:23⟧.†
SYN.: εἰκών (q.v.), ὁμοίωσις.

G3674.b:
⟪ὁμοῦ⟫, adv.
(< ὁμός), ⟪together⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ prop., of place: ⟦John 21:2|Jo 21:2⟧, ⟦Acts 2:1|Ac 2:1⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ without idea of place: ⟦John 4:36|Jo 4:36⟧ ⟦John 20:4|20:4⟧.†

G3694.b:
⟪ὀπίσω⟫, adv. of place and time,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אַחֲרֵי⁩, ⁨אַחַר⁩ and cogn. forms;]
⟪1.⟫ prop., as in cl., adv.,
	⟪(a)⟫ of time (not in NT);
	⟪(b)⟫ of place, ⟪back⟫, ⟪behind⟫, ⟪after⟫: ⟦Matthew 24:18|Mt 24:18⟧, ⟦Luke 7:38|Lk 7:38⟧; τὰ ὀ., ⟦Philippians 3:13|Phl 3:13⟧; εἰς τὰ ὀ., ⟦Mark 13:16|Mk 13:16⟧, ⟦Luke 9:62|Lk 9:62⟧ ⟦Luke 17:31|17:31⟧, ⟦John 6:66|Jo 6:66⟧ ⟦John 18:6|18:6⟧ ⟦John 20:14|20:14⟧.
⟪2.⟫ By a usage not found in cl., and in LXX representing the Heb. prep. ⁨אַחֲרֵי⁩ (Bl., § 40, 8; Thackeray, Gr., 46 f.), but also prob. general in vernacular (M, Pr., 99), as prep. c. gen.;
	⟪(a)⟫ of time, ⟪after⟫: ⟦Matthew 3:11|Mt 3:11⟧, ⟦Mark 1:7|Mk 1:7⟧, ⟦John 1:15|Jo 1:15⟧, ⟦John 1:27|27⟧, ⟦John 1:30|30⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of place, ⟪behind⟫, ⟪after⟫: ⟦Matthew 4:19|Mt 4:19⟧ ⟦Matthew 10:38|10:38⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:23|16:23⟧, ⟦Matthew 16:24|24⟧, ⟦Mark 1:17|Mk 1:17⟧, ⟦Mark 1:20|20⟧ ⟦Mark 8:33|8:33⟧, ⟦Mark 8:34|34⟧, ⟦Luke 9:23|Lk 9:23⟧ ⟦Luke 14:27|14:27⟧ ⟦Luke 19:14|19:14⟧ ⟦Luke 21:8|21:8⟧, ⟦2 Peter 2:10|II Pe 2:10⟧, ⟦Jude 1:7|Ju 7⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:10|Re 1:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 12:15|12:15⟧; in constr. praegn. (v. Swete on ⟦Revelation 13:3|Re 13:3⟧), ⟦John 12:19|Jo 12:19⟧, ⟦Acts 5:17|Ac 5:17⟧ ⟦Acts 20:30|20:30⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:15|I Ti 5:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 13:3|Re 13:3⟧.†
